(21, 47, 11, 'hihi', 'Hello! It seems there might have been a typo in your message. How can I assist you with your itinerary for the 2D Culture & Food Getaway in Johor and Kelantan? Are you looking to understand or improve any part of your planned route?', '2026-05-11 12:04:03'),
(22, 49, 11, 'Reply as an AI chatbot in one short sentence.', 'Your route is planned to visit Kacang Pool Haji Restauran at 10:33 AM for food, followed by a visit to Johor Bahru Old Chinese Temple at 12:13 PM for heritage attraction. The travel time between these two points is estimated to be around 10 minutes.', '2026-05-11 12:06:11'),
(23, 47, 11, 'hihi', 'Hello! It seems there might have been a typo in your message. How can I assist you with your itinerary for the 2D Culture & Food Getaway in Johor and Kelantan? Here’s a brief overview of your planned activities:\n\n- **Day 1:**\n  - Visit Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup (Nature Park) in Johor Bahru. Opening hours are from 9:00 AM to 4:00 PM.\n  - For lunch, head to Mee Rebus (Johor Style), located near the nature park. It\'s open from 7:30 AM to 9:30 PM.\n\n- **Day 2:**\n  - Enjoy a meal at Kacang Pool Haji Restauran in Johor Bahru. They are open from 7:00 AM to 12:00 AM.\n  \nIf you need more detailed route instructions or have any questions, please let me know!', '2026-05-11 12:09:36'),
(24, 47, 11, 'Act as my travel AI chatbot and explain this itinerary.', 'Here\'s a breakdown of your 2-day cultural and food getaway itinerary in Johor and Kelantan:\n\n- **Day 1:**\n  - **Morning:** Visit Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup (Nature Park) located near Johor Bahru. It\'s open from 9 AM to 4 PM.\n  - Afternoon: Enjoy Mee Rebus (Johor Style), a local restaurant known for its authentic dishes, in Johor Bahru. The restaurant is open from 7:30 AM to 9:30 PM.\n  - Evening: Explore Kacang Pool Haji Restauran for more culinary delights in Johor Bahru, which operates from 7 AM to midnight.\n\n- **Day 2:** \n  - No specific attractions are planned for Day 2. Consider visiting other places of interest or relaxing based on your preferences.\n\nPlease note the distances and travel times are estimated. You might want to check a map for precise directions. Enjoy your trip!', '2026-05-11 12:09:50'),
(25, 47, 11, 'How can I improve this itinerary within my budget?', 'To stay within your $200 budget, consider the following improvements:\n\n- Reduce travel time from Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup to Mee Rebus (Johor Style) by 49 minutes.\n- Lower food costs: Skip one of the meal stops or reduce its cost by choosing a less expensive restaurant option.\n\nYou can also explore nearby attractions within Johor for free, like parks and beaches.', '2026-05-11 12:10:15'),
(26, 47, 11, 'what is the suggestion for hotel', 'For your itinerary, there are no specific recommendations for hotels included in the provided context. Here are some suggestions based on your preferences:\n\n- For overnight stays, consider staying in Johor Bahru or other cities within Johor and Kelantan.\n- You could look into budget-friendly options like hostels or guesthouses near attractions such as Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup and Mee Rebus (Johor Style).\n- For a more comfortable stay, you might consider booking mid-range hotels in Johor Bahru.\n\nPlease check reviews and amenities to find the best fit for your budget and preferences.', '2026-05-11 12:10:37'),
(28, 46, 11, 'hi', 'Hello! For your itinerary in Johor, you have planned two cultural and food-focused visits. Here\'s a summary of what you\'ve got so far:\n\n- **Day 1**: Visit \"Mee Rebus (Johor Style)\" for Mee Rebus, which is located in Johor Bahru. The cost is RM15 and it operates from 7:30 AM to 9:30 PM.\n- **Day 2**: Head over to \"Kacang Pool Haji Restauran\" also in Johor Bahru for more dining experiences. This place costs RM8 and has opening hours from 7 AM to 12 AM.\n\nIf you need any route suggestions or cost estimations, feel free to ask!', '2026-05-12 18:39:50'),
(29, 46, 11, 'Act as my travel AI chatbot and explain this trip summary.', 'This itinerary for one day in Johor, Malaysia focuses on culture and food experiences. You\'ll start your day with Mee Rebus (Johor Style), a popular dish served in the Johor Bahru area. After that, you\'re heading to Kacang Pool Haji Restauran where you can enjoy more Malaysian cuisine.\n\nThe cost for these activities is estimated at RM23 out of an estimated total budget of RM200. The travel time between these two places is about 6 minutes by car. Both restaurants are open from 7:30 AM to 9:30 PM and from 7 AM to midnight respectively.\n\nFor practical improvements, consider checking the opening hours for any potential changes or if you prefer dining at a specific time. You might also want to explore other food spots in Johor Bahru for a more diverse culinary experience.', '2026-05-12 18:40:22'),
(30, 47, 11, 'hi', 'Hello! I can help you plan your itinerary between Johor and Kelantan for the 2D Culture & Food Getaway in February 2026. Let\'s start by looking at your attractions, food experiences, and transportation details. How do you feel about this initial setup? Do you need any adjustments or additional information?', '2026-05-19 04:13:21'),
(31, 47, 11, 'How can I improve this itinerary within my budget?', 'You might consider reducing the cost of your stay in Johor Bahru by looking for cheaper accommodation options or exploring free attractions nearby. Also, you could extend your visit to Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup if it\'s not essential to visit it on day 1, as it offers more activities and is less crowded during off-peak times.', '2026-05-19 04:13:24'),
(32, 47, 11, 'ok can please arrange the itinerary for me', 'Sure, here\'s a revised itinerary based on your preferences:\n\n**Day 1:**\n- Start from Johor Bahru (Johor) and head to Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup. The cost is RM25.\n- Travel time by car is approximately 49 minutes.\n- Opening hours for attractions are 9:00 am – 4:00 pm.\n\n**Day 1 Evening:**\n- After visiting Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup, head to Mee Rebus (Johor Style) in Johor Bahru. The cost is RM15.\n- Travel time by car is about 49 minutes.\n- Opening hours are from 7:30 am – 9:30 pm.\n\n**Day 2:**\n- Visit Kacang Pool Haji Restauran (Johor Bahru) for some local cuisine. The cost is RM8.\n- Travel time by car is about 6 minutes, and opening hours are from 7am - 12pm.\n\nEnjoy your getaway!', '2026-05-19 04:13:59'),
(33, 47, 11, 'noooo, i need more than that. no just this 3, but also include other cultural places', 'Sure! Here\'s an additional cultural place you can visit in Johor:\n\n4. Taman Negara Johor - This is a smaller version of the famous Taman Negara and offers similar natural beauty and wildlife experiences.\n\nFor Kelantan, consider visiting:\n5. Kampung Matang Melayu - A traditional Malay village where you can learn about local culture and customs.\n\nRemember to check opening hours and distances for these places as they might not be exactly like the previous ones. Enjoy your cultural getaway!', '2026-05-19 04:15:09'),
(34, 47, 11, 'noooo what kelantan?', 'If you\'re interested in Kelantan, we can include attractions and activities that reflect its unique culture and natural beauty. For your second day, consider visiting Taman Negara Kelantan or exploring the local markets like Pasar Besar Chetti for food and cultural experiences. Would you like to add any of these options?', '2026-05-19 04:15:41'),
(35, 47, 11, 'no i dont want kelantan', 'Understood, you\'ll be focusing on attractions and dining in Johor now. Here\'s a revised itinerary:\n\n- Day 1: Visit Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup (Nature Park) at Pontian, Johor.\n- Day 2: Enjoy Mee Rebus (Johor Style) in Johor Bahru for lunch.\n\nYou can explore more of Johor or find other dining options as you wish.', '2026-05-19 04:15:54'),
(36, 47, 11, 'can u arrange for my day 2 since my day 2 is empty', 'Sure, I can help you with your itinerary for Day 2. You have a choice of dining options in Johor Bahru that cater to different preferences and cuisines. Here are some suggestions:\n\n1. **Mee Rebus (Johor Style)** - This place offers traditional Johor-style mee rebus, which is a popular dish made with thick rice noodles in a savory coconut milk base. It’s known for its authentic taste.\n\n2. **Kacang Pool Haji Restauran** - Located in the heart of Johor Bahru, this restaurant serves various types of kacang tai (green pea soup) dishes and other local favorites. It\'s a great spot to try traditional Malaysian fare.\n\nWould you like more information on these options or should I suggest another place?', '2026-05-19 04:16:27'),
(37, 47, 11, 'and extra?', 'You could consider visiting the Taman Negara in Kelantan, which is about 28 km from Johor Bahru. This park offers a variety of activities like trekking and wildlife watching. It\'s also a great place to learn more about nature.\n\nFor food options, you might want to explore local markets or try other dishes specific to Kelantan. The area is known for its unique cuisine that combines Malay, Chinese, and Indian influences.\n\nRemember to check the opening hours and distance for Taman Negara as they are estimated data.', '2026-05-19 04:16:51'),
(38, 47, 11, 'How can I improve this itinerary within my budget?', 'You could consider removing the travel time and distance for the Mee Rebus (Johor Style) stop, as it might be included in your current budget. Instead, you could allocate some of that cost to a different attraction or food spot closer to your accommodation to save on transportation costs. Another option is to look for cheaper dining options within Johor Bahru where Kacang Pool Haji Restauran (Johor Bahru) is located.', '2026-05-19 04:32:24'),
(39, 47, 11, 'the nearest places from yesterday', 'The nearest place from the previous day is Mee Rebus (Johor Style) in Johor Bahru, which is approximately 49.44 kilometers away and a travel time of about 49 minutes by car. It\'s classified as an attraction under food category.', '2026-05-19 04:33:51'),
(40, 47, 11, 'yesterday already have, provide me more', 'You\'ve included Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup and Mee Rebus (Johor Style) in your itinerary. Here are some additional options for you:\n\nFor the third day, you might consider visiting Pasir Garam Nature Park in Johor. It\'s known for its beautiful beaches and natural scenery.\n\nAlso, if you\'re interested in exploring more of Johor Bahru, you could visit the Chenderoh Waterfall or the Batu Gajah Cave.\n\nRemember to check opening hours and distances as these can vary. You can use your confirmation cards for further details if needed.', '2026-05-19 04:34:42'),
(41, 47, 11, 'ok', 'You have the following itinerary for day 1 in Johor:\n- Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup: nature attraction, cost RM25, travel time 49 minutes, opening hours 9.00 am–4.00 pm.\n\nFor day 2, you will need to choose another attraction or activity as none are specified in your preferences list for day 2. Please let me know if you would like to modify or add any stops.', '2026-05-19 04:34:58'),
(42, 47, 11, 'hi who are u', 'I am your travel assistant here to help plan your itinerary for the 2-day culture and food getaway in Johor and Kelantan. How can I assist you today?', '2026-05-19 04:41:45');
