(3, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"attraction_price\",\"report_title\":\"Attraction and Price Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"Management Report\\n\\nExecutive Summary\\nThe database snapshot for the period from All time shows a diverse range of cultural and tourist activities with varying levels of engagement. Active attractions total 280, including Free Places (152). The highest recorded price is RM 225.00, while the average price across all active places is RM 8.34.\\n\\nIn terms of cost insights, the most used attraction in itineraries was \\\"Mee Rebus (Johor Style)\\\" from Johor Bahru, used by 7 people at a total cost of RM15.00. The highest-priced attractions were found in Sabah and Kuala Lumpur, with Monsopiad Heritage Villa\"}', '2026-05-23 13:29:58'),
(4, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"overview\",\"report_title\":\"System Overview Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"Admin Report\\n\\nExecutive Summary\\nThis report provides an overview of the system\'s performance and user engagement across various metrics. Over all time, we have 7 registered travellers with 8 generated trips. There are 280 active cultural places in our database. The AI assistant has logged 39 questions since its inception.\\n\\nIn terms of trip generation, during May 2026, the system generated 5 trips worth RM1,553.25 and in January 2026, it produced 3 trips costing RM216.04. The content suggestion process has a status breakdown where 4 records are approved, 1 is pending review, and 1 is rejected.\\n\"}', '2026-05-23 13:32:16'),
(5, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"overview\",\"report_title\":\"System Overview Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. System Overview Summary:\\n- Total registered travellers: 7 active users.\\n- Total generated trips: 8, filtered by the selected period.\\n- Active cultural places: 280 records.\\n\\n2. User, Trip, and Cultural Data Status:\\n- No preference records available in the provided data.\\n- Shared itinerary links count: 1 link shared.\\n\\n3. Operational Gaps Shown by the Report:\\n- There are no explicit operational gaps highlighted in this report type, but the number of active cultural places is high (280), indicating a need for user engagement and trip generation to maximize their potential.\\n\\n4. Admin Actions for\"}', '2026-05-23 17:06:51'),
(6, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"overview\",\"report_title\":\"System Overview Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. System Overview Summary:\\n- Total registered travellers: 7\\n- Generated trips: 8 (filtered by selected period)\\n- Active cultural places: 280\\n- AI questions logged: 39\\n\\n2. User, Trip, and Cultural Data Status:\\n- No specific details provided about user preferences or itineraries generated.\\n\\n3. Operational Gaps Shown by the Report:\\n- There are no significant gaps identified in the data provided for operational improvements.\\n\\n4. Admin Actions for System Readiness:\\n- Ensure that all cultural places remain active and accessible.\\n- Monitor AI question logs to address any issues with user queries.\\n- \"}', '2026-05-23 17:06:57'),
(7, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"user_preferences\",\"report_title\":\"User Preference Analysis Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. Preference Summary\\nThe user preferences report shows that out of all preference records, \\\"Food\\\" and \\\"Johor\\\" are the top interests and desired states respectively.\\n\\n2. Highest and Lowest User Preferences\\n- Highest: Food (6 selections), Johor (6 selections)\\n- Lowest: Festival (2 selections), Museum (2 selections)\\n\\n3. Budget, Duration, and Transport Pattern\\n- Average budget across all preference records is RM 1,631.71.\\n- Most users prefer public transport with an average budget of RM 1,000.00 per trip.\\n- Budget ranges:\\n- RM800-RM1499 (3 selections, RM 1,000.00 average)\\n- Budget above RM1500 (3\"}', '2026-05-23 17:08:24'),
(8, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"destination_demand\",\"report_title\":\"Destination Demand Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. Destination Demand Summary:\\n- The most desired state is Johor with 6 preference selections.\\n- The least desired state has no selection records (Kedah).\\n- Johor is the highest generator of destination items, producing 60 itinerary items.\\n\\n2. Desired States and Districts:\\n- Users have shown interest in states like Johor but not in Kedah or Perak.\\n- There are no districts listed as desired by users, indicating a need for more targeted marketing efforts.\\n\\n3. Actual Generated Destination Pattern:\\n- In terms of state-level demand, only one itinerary has been generated from the least desired distr\"}', '2026-05-23 17:09:19'),
(9, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"destination_demand\",\"report_title\":\"Destination Demand Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. Destination Demand Summary:\\n- Most Desired State: Johor with 6 preference selections.\\n- Least Desired State: Kedah with no selection.\\n\\n2. Desired States and Districts:\\n- The system has generated itineraries for all states except Kedah, which is the least desired state by users.\\n- No districts have been selected as most or least desirable by users.\\n\\n3. Actual Generated Destination Pattern:\\n- 8 Itineraries were generated in Johor with a total of 60 items.\\n- All these itineraries are centered around the district of Johor Bahru, which is also where all itinerary items are located within Johor.\"}', '2026-05-23 17:09:27'),
(10, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"attraction_price\",\"report_title\":\"Attraction and Price Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. Cultural Place and Price Summary:\\n- Total Active Attractions: 280\\n- Free Places: 152 (61.4% of total)\\n- Highest Price: RM 225.00\\n- Average Price: RM 8.34\\n\\n2. Category and Price Coverage:\\n- Heritage: 65 places, average price RM 2.06\\n- Nature: 64 places, average price RM 6.80\\n- Food: 63 places, average price RM 18.89\\n- Culture: 40 places, highest price RM 225.00 (average RM 10.75)\\n- Museum: 28 places, average price RM 5.18\\n\\n3. Data Completeness Issues:\\n- Places without coordinates: 0\\n- Places without image: 0\\n- Places without opening hours: 13\\n- Places without visit duration: 0\\n\\n4. Admin Acti\"}', '2026-05-23 17:09:43'),
(11, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"ai_usage\",\"report_title\":\"AI Usage Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"AI Usage Summary:\\n- Total AI Questions: 39\\n- Assistant Responses: 39\\n- Itinerary Questions: 21\\n- Active AI Users: 1\\n\\nQuestion Intent Pattern:\\n- General question: 27\\n- Cost and budget: 5\\n- Route writing: 4\\n- Improvement suggestion: 3\\n\\nMost Active AI User:\\nPECK JIAN HAO asked a total of 39 questions, the last on May 19, 2026 at 12:41.\"}', '2026-05-23 17:12:32'),
(12, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"user_preferences\",\"report_title\":\"User Preference Analysis Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. Preference Summary\\nThe report indicates that out of the total preference records, users have selected interests such as Food (6 selections), Culture (4 selections), Heritage (3 selections), Nature (3 selections), Festival (2 selections), Museum (2 selections), and Shopping (2 selections). The top desired state for user preferences is Johor with 6 selections.\\n\\n2. Highest and Lowest User Preferences\\nThe highest user interests are Food, Culture, Heritage, Nature, Festival, Museum, and Shopping, each selected 6 times. The lowest user interests include Festival, Museum, Shopping, Heritage, Natur\"}', '2026-05-23 17:16:56'),
(13, 1, 'generate_ai_report', 'admin_report', NULL, '{\"report_type\":\"attraction_price\",\"report_title\":\"Attraction and Price Report\",\"period\":\"All time\",\"summary\":\"1. Cultural Place and Price Summary:\\n- There are 280 active cultural places in the database, with an average price of RM 8.34.\\n\\n2. Category and Price Coverage:\\n- The most active category is nature (64 places), followed by food (63 places) and heritage (65 places).\\n- The highest price for any place is RM 225.00, which can be found at Monsopiad Heritage Village in Sabah.\\n\\n3. Data Completeness Issues:\\n- There are no issues with coordinates or images for cultural places.\\n- Places have opening hours and visit duration information available.\\n\\n4. Admin Actions for Knowledge Base Quality:\\n- Ensure tha\"}', '2026-05-23 17:23:19');
INSERT INTO `cultural_places` (`place_id`, `state`, `district`, `category`, `name`, `description`, `address`, `latitude`, `longitude`, `opening_hours`, `festival_start_date`, `festival_end_date`, `estimated_cost`, `entrance_fee`, `is_free`, `image_url`, `halal_status`, `is_outdoor`, `visit_duration_min`, `best_time_to_visit`, `dress_code_required`, `website_url`, `phone_number`, `avg_rating`, `rating`, `is_active`, `created_by_admin_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1, 'Johor', 'Johor Bahru', 'food', 'Kacang Pool Haji Restauran (Johor Bahru)', 'Local Johor breakfast dish, commonly served with bread.Kacang Pool Haji Restaurant is an iconic and must-visit culinary destination in Johor Bahru, famous for its signature dish, Kacang Pool Haji, which has been captivating the palates of many visitors since 2009. The restaurant offers a rich, rich, and satisfying Johor dining experience, perfect for breakfast, lunch, dinner, or even a late-night snack.', '12, Jalan Dato Jaafar, Taman Dato Onn, 80350 Johor Bahru, Johor Darul Ta\'zim', 1.4907395, 103.7515533, '7am - 12am', NULL, NULL, 8.00, 8.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1766837821_4033.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-15 01:26:21', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(2, 'Johor', 'Johor Bahru', 'food', 'Mee Rebus (Johor Style)', 'Mee Rebus Selera Johor (Warisan Keluarga Hj. Wahid) is famous for its authentic Johor dishes based on family recipes passed down through generations since 1948. It serves a variety of iconic Malaysian dishes, with a main focus on the mee rebus with a thick and flavorful peanut sauce. Traditional Johor-style mee rebus with rich gravy.', 'Johor Bahru, Johor', 1.4927000, 103.7414000, '7:30 am–9:30 pm', NULL, NULL, 15.00, 15.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1766835810_7693.png', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-15 01:26:21', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(3, 'Johor', 'Batu Pahat', 'heritage', 'Chong Long Gong Temple', 'Historic temple representing Chinese community heritage.Chong Long Gong Temple is a unique and vibrant Chinese temple located by the sea in the Kampung Segenting fishing village of Batu Pahat, Johor, Malaysia. It is famous for its large arapaima fish, believed to bring good fortune to those who touch them.', '81, Kampung Segenting, Batu Pahat, 83030 Bandar Penggaram, Johor', 1.7836877, 102.8926308, '9:00 AM - 6:00 PM', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_1766836350_7759.webp', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-15 01:26:21', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(4, 'Johor', 'Johor Bahru', 'museum', 'Johor Bahru Chinese Heritage Museum', 'Museum showcasing Johor Bahru Chinese heritage and history.The Johor Bahru Chinese Heritage Museum (Malay: Muzium Warisan Tionghua Johor Bahru) is a museum in Johor Bahru, Johor, Malaysia. The museum is about the history of Chinese community in Johor Bahru. Collections in the museum include documents, music instruments, old money, photos, porcelain etc. It showcases the early days of the Chinese settlement in Johor Bahru, their history, culture, traditions and occupations.', 'Johor Bahru, Johor', 1.4579000, 103.7646000, '9.00 a.m. - 5.00 p.m. except Mondays', NULL, NULL, 6.00, 6.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1766836057_2242.webp', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-15 01:26:21', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(5, 'Kedah', 'Kota Setar', 'nature', 'Gunung Jerai', 'Popular mountain attraction with scenic views. Gunung Jerai is the highest peak in Kedah, Malaysia, a unique island-shaped mountain (inselberg) that is easily visible from afar, serving as a landmark and sea navigation since ancient times, now a popular tourist destination with a resort at the top, recreational activities such as hiking, cycling, paragliding, as well as rich geological and botanical treasures, with panoramic views towards the rice fields and the Straits of Malacca.', 'Yan, Kedah', 5.7887000, 100.4246000, '08:00-18:00', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_1766835360_5565.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-15 01:26:21', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(6, 'Kedah', 'Kota Setar', 'museum', 'Kedah State Museum', 'Museum presenting history and culture of Kedah. The history of the establishment of the Kedah State Museum began on 3 February 1957, known as the Kedah History Museum. The museum, located on the ground floor of the Balai Besar, Alor Setar, was officiated by YAB Tan Sri Tunku Ismail bin Tunku Yahya, the 2nd Menteri Besar of Kedah Darul Aman. The increase in the number of collections caused the museum to be moved to its own building (next to the new museum building) on ​​the Darul Aman Highway, Bakar Bata on 30 December 1961. In July 1964, the Kedah History Museum was changed its name to the Kedah State Museum.\r\n\r\nGiven the good response from the public, the State Government agreed to build the current building in 1997. This building houses an exhibition hall, workshop, library, and mini theatrette. There are 10 permanent exhibition galleries such as the Cultural Hall, the History Hall, the Nature Hall, the Heroes Hall, the Transport Hall, the Weapons Hall, the Manuscript Hall, the Textile Hall, the Arts and Crafts Hall and the Language and Literature Corner. Apart from that, its facilities have also been improved by providing an elevator, cafeteria, car parking and public toilets.', 'Alor Setar, Kedah', 6.1210000, 100.3680000, '09:00-17:00', NULL, NULL, 5.00, 5.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1766835098_6695.webp', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-15 01:26:21', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(7, 'Kedah', 'Kota Setar', 'food', 'Din Laksa Teluk Kechai', 'Famous Kedah laksa experience.This legendary Laksa in 1967 when it was sold by Din himself on his gerek going from house to house.', 'No 246 Batu 4 1/4 jalan kuala kedah, Alor Setar 06600 Malaysia', 6.0949606, 100.3206236, '3:00 PM - 8:00 PM', NULL, NULL, 15.00, 15.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1766831415_1464.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2025-12-15 01:26:21', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(8, 'Johor', 'Pontian', 'nature', 'Taman Negara Johor Pulau Kukup', 'Pulau Kukup is one of the world’s largest uninhabited mangrove islands and a protected national park in Johor. The island is well known for its wooden boardwalks, rich mangrove ecosystem, and traditional fishing village culture, offering visitors a unique combination of natural conservation and cultural heritage.', 'Lot 1319, Mukim, 82300 Kukup, Johor Darul Ta\'zim', 1.3225724, 103.4283275, '9.00 am–4.00 pm', NULL, NULL, 25.00, 25.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1766813513_1914.webp', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-23 23:50:41', '2026-05-12 19:48:50'),
(9, 'Johor', 'Johor Bahru', 'heritage', 'Johor Bahru Old Chinese Temple (柔佛古庙)', 'One of the oldest Chinese temples in Johor Bahru, serving as an important spiritual and cultural landmark for the local Chinese community. It is closely associated with the annual Johor Bahru Chingay procession, where different Chinese clans and associations participate in traditional rituals, performances, and parades. The temple reflects the city’s multicultural heritage and is often visited by travellers who want to experience local religious traditions, community history, and the atmosphere of the old town area.（柔佛新山历史悠久的华人庙宇之一，是当地华人社群重要的信仰与文化地标。它与每年新山古庙游神（Chingay）密切相关，活动期间各籍贯与会馆参与传统祭祀、表演与游行，展现地方社群的凝聚力与多元文化。游客可在此了解本地宗教习俗、社区历史，并感受老城区的文化氛围。）', 'Lot 653, Jalan Trus, Bandar Johor Bahru, 80000 Johor Bahru, Johor Darul Ta\'zim', 1.4606803, 103.7630595, '7:00 AM – 6:00 PM', NULL, NULL, 20.00, 20.00, 0, 'uploads/places/suggest_1766814848_5261.webp', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-26 21:54:44', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(10, 'Selangor', 'Petaling Jaya', 'nature', 'Forest Research Institute Malaysia (FRIM)', 'Forest park with canopy walk, nature trails, and educational eco-tourism experiences.', 'Forest Research Institute Malaysia (FRIM), 52109 Kepong, Selangor, Malaysia', 3.2353390, 101.6342690, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_10_169294a803_20260105_120730_5e4700.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(11, 'Selangor', 'Petaling Jaya', 'festival', 'Thaipusam at Batu Caves', 'Major religious-cultural festival with pilgrimages, rituals, and vibrant community participation.', 'Batu Caves Temple, Gombak, 68100 Batu Caves, Selangor, Malaysia', 3.2374000, 101.6839070, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_11_30123df278_20260105_120731_8f5f34.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(12, 'Sarawak', 'Miri', 'heritage', 'Niah Caves (Niah National Park)', 'Archaeological and cultural heritage caves complex known for early human history and cave exploration.', 'Niah National Park, Batu Niah, 98200 Miri, Sarawak, Malaysia', 3.8083000, 113.7755000, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_12_85ade11fe5_20260105_120734_5496bb.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(13, 'Sarawak', 'Kuching', 'culture', 'Sarawak Cultural Village', 'Living museum showcasing Sarawak ethnic groups with traditional houses and cultural performances.', 'Sarawak Cultural Village, Pantai Damai, Santubong, 93752 Kuching, Sarawak, Malaysia', 1.7497100, 110.3169800, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_13_1dada0c29d_20260105_120735_8c494b.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(14, 'Sarawak', 'Kuching', 'festival', 'Rainforest World Music Festival', 'Signature music and cultural festival combining world music showcases with local cultural elements.', 'Sarawak Cultural Village, Pantai Damai, Santubong, 93752 Kuching, Sarawak, Malaysia', 1.7497100, 110.3169800, '', '2026-06-26', '2026-06-28', 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_1766958248_6687.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, '', '', NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-05-23 06:00:39'),
(15, 'Sarawak', 'Kuching', 'nature', 'Gunung Mulu National Park', 'UNESCO natural site famous for limestone karst formations, rainforest, and extensive cave systems.', 'Gunung Mulu National Park HQ, 98070 Mulu, Sarawak, Malaysia', 4.1320000, 114.9190000, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_15_d451eb69ae_20260105_121459_5c8d18.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(16, 'Perak', 'Hulu Perak', 'heritage', 'Archaeological Heritage of the Lenggong Valley', 'UNESCO-listed archaeological landscape featuring significant prehistoric findings and sites.', 'Lenggong Valley (Lembah Lenggong), 33400 Lenggong, Perak, Malaysia', 5.0557500, 100.9625300, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_16_28a30c79d0_20260105_121504_08dcd3.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, 'https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1396/', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-05-13 02:39:32'),
(17, 'Penang', 'Timur Laut', 'heritage', 'Cheong Fatt Tze Mansion (The Blue Mansion)', 'Straits Chinese heritage mansion offering guided tours highlighting architecture and Peranakan influence.', '14, Leith Street, 10200 George Town, Penang, Malaysia', 5.4213194, 100.3352500, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_17_0f1d7f3b50_20260105_120749_69e67c.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(18, 'Penang', 'Timur Laut', 'festival', 'George Town Festival', 'Annual arts and culture festival featuring performances, exhibitions, and heritage-focused programs. The 2026 George Town Festival (GTF) is an annual arts and culture event held in Penang, Malaysia, commemorating the city\'s UNESCO World Heritage Site designation. The 17th edition runs from August 1 to 9, 2026, under the theme \"Beyond Boundaries,\" offering a vibrant lineup of theatre, dance, and visual arts', 'George Town Festival Office, 1st Floor, 86 Lebuh Armenian, 10200 George Town, Penang, Malaysia', 5.4154392, 100.3370691, '', '2026-08-01', '2026-08-09', 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_1779516592_6208.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, '', '', NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-05-23 06:09:52'),
(19, 'Melaka', 'Melaka Tengah', 'museum', 'Baba & Nyonya Heritage Museum', 'Peranakan house museum showcasing traditional lifestyle, artifacts, and cultural history in historic Melaka.', '48 & 50, Jalan Tun Tan Cheng Lock, 75200 Melaka, Malaysia', 2.1952670, 102.2466570, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_19_c023100102_20260105_120755_1fe0c4.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(20, 'Kuala Lumpur', 'City Centre (KLCC)', 'museum', 'Islamic Arts Museum Malaysia (IAMM)', 'Major museum showcasing Islamic art, design, and cultural heritage collections.', 'Islamic Arts Museum Malaysia, Jalan Lembah Perdana, 50480 Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia', 3.1418340, 101.6886180, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_20_4fd8bba161_20260105_121510_b26c9a.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(21, 'Kuala Lumpur', 'City Centre (KLCC)', 'museum', 'Muzium Negara (National Museum)', 'National museum presenting Malaysia history, culture, and nation-building narratives.', 'Muzium Negara, Jalan Damansara, 50566 Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia', 3.1379960, 101.6870430, '09:00-17:00', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_21_60f3eb5978_20260105_121514_5d3aa2.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(22, 'Terengganu', 'Kuala Terengganu', 'shopping', 'Pasar Payang', 'Traditional market for local products such as textiles, snacks, souvenirs, and crafts.', 'Pasar Payang, Jalan Sultan Zainal Abidin, 20200 Kuala Terengganu, Terengganu, Malaysia', 5.3300000, 103.1380000, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_22_c8b317e8dd_20260105_120808_88a923.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(23, 'Sabah', 'Kota Kinabalu', 'culture', 'Monsopiad Heritage Village', 'The Monsopiad Heritage Village is a private living museum in Penampang, Sabah, established on the historical site where the legendary Kadazandusun warrior and headhunter, Monsopiad, lived over 300 years ago. Managed by his direct descendants, the village serves to preserve and document the traditions, beliefs, and rich heritage of Sabah’s largest indigenous group. Visitors are offered a deep dive into the past through immersive storytelling, traditional architecture, and interactive displays that showcase the lifestyle and spiritual practices of the Kadazandusun community.\r\n \r\nKey Highlights:\r\n-House of Skulls (Siou Do Mohoing): The village\'s centerpiece, which houses 42 \"trophies\" — the actual skulls of enemies defeated by Monsopiad.\r\n-Massive Monolith (Gintutun do Mohoing): A sacred stone standing four meters tall, believed to be inhabited by spirits and used in grand rituals.\r\n-Cultural Performances: Traditional music and dance shows, including the Sumazau and Magunatip (bamboo) dances, often featuring audience participation.\r\n-Interactive Activities: Hands-on experiences such as blowpipe shooting, fire-making, catapult use, and walking on bamboo stilts.\r\n-Traditional Delicacies: Opportunities to sample local rice wine (lihing or tapai), traditional snacks, and for the adventurous, live sago worms (butod).\r\n-Heritage Structures: Authentic replicas of traditional dwellings, including a grainery (tangkob) and the main house dedicated to Monsopiad’s legacy.', 'Kampung Kuai Kandazon, Jalan Putatan Ramayah, 89507 Penampang, Sabah', 5.8888540, 116.0792531, 'Monday to Sunday, 9 am–4:30 pm', NULL, NULL, 225.00, 225.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_23_95717a344d_20260105_120813_bd78dc.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-05-23 03:25:01'),
(24, 'Sabah', 'Kota Kinabalu', 'nature', 'Kinabalu Park', 'UNESCO natural site known for biodiversity and as the gateway to Mount Kinabalu.', 'Kinabalu Park Headquarters, 89307 Ranau, Sabah, Malaysia', 6.0055351, 116.5422225, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_24_7be148a719_20260105_120836_02a8a1.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2025-12-27 01:36:07', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(28, 'Kelantan', 'Kota Bharu', 'museum', 'Istana Jahar (Kelantan Traditional Royal Ceremonies Museum)', 'Royal palace museum featuring Kelantanese royal ceremonies, traditional customs, and cultural exhibits.', 'Jalan Sultan, Bandar Kota Bharu, 15000 Kota Bharu, Kelantan, Malaysia', 6.1315200, 102.2371300, 'Daily 8:30 AM–5:45 PM (Closed Fridays)', NULL, NULL, 2.00, 2.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_28_7acb892af4_20260114_152526_98645c.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 07:09:09', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
