(39, 'Putrajaya', 'Putrajaya', 'food', 'Medan Selera Presint 9 (Putrajaya)', 'Lokasi makanan tempatan dengan pelbagai gerai: masakan Melayu, mi, nasi, dan minuman. Sesuai untuk pengalaman gastronomi harian dengan bajet sederhana.', 'Presint 9, 62250 Putrajaya, Wilayah Persekutuan Putrajaya, Malaysia', 2.8968000, 101.6909000, 'Daily 08:00–22:00', NULL, NULL, 20.00, 20.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1768404351_3690.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 15:22:24', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(40, 'Putrajaya', 'Putrajaya', 'festival', 'Anjung Floria Putrajaya', 'Lokasi utama penganjuran Royal Floria Putrajaya (festival bunga) dan acara bermusim. Kawasan landskap sesuai untuk pameran dan fotografi.', 'Jalan Anjung Floria, Presint 4, 62000 Putrajaya, Wilayah Persekutuan Putrajaya, Malaysia', 2.9126110, 101.6771720, 'Daily 07:00–22:00 (park area; event schedules are seasonal)', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_40_b6b991191b_20260114_162259_a0fc88.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 15:22:24', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(41, 'Putrajaya', 'Putrajaya', 'nature', 'Taman Botani Putrajaya (Putrajaya Botanical Garden)', 'Taman botani yang luas dengan zon landskap, denai berjalan kaki dan ruang rekreasi. Sesuai untuk riadah dan pembelajaran flora.', 'Lebuh Perdana Barat, Presint 1, 62000 Putrajaya, Wilayah Persekutuan Putrajaya, Malaysia', 2.9448069, 101.6955157, 'Daily 07:00–19:00', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_41_c88b978354_20260114_162303_bd4af5.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 15:22:24', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(42, 'Putrajaya', 'Putrajaya', 'nature', 'Taman Wetland Putrajaya (Putrajaya Wetlands Park)', 'Kawasan wetland buatan yang menyokong biodiversiti dan pendidikan ekologi. Sesuai untuk pemerhatian alam dan aktiviti santai.', 'Jalan P11, Presint 13, 62000 Putrajaya, Wilayah Persekutuan Putrajaya, Malaysia', 2.9618472, 101.6955194, 'Daily 07:00–19:00', NULL, NULL, 10.00, 10.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_42_2af8e4dc28_20260114_162305_f02425.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 15:22:24', '2026-05-09 16:48:45'),
(43, 'Putrajaya', 'Putrajaya', 'shopping', 'Alamanda Shopping Centre', 'Pusat beli-belah utama di Putrajaya dengan pelbagai kedai runcit, F&B dan kemudahan keluarga.', 'Jalan Alamanda 2, Presint 1, 62000 Putrajaya, Wilayah Persekutuan Putrajaya, Malaysia', 2.9395140, 101.7111320, 'Daily 10:00–22:00', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_43_8fa0ae2b38_20260114_162309_10fc4c.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 15:22:24', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(44, 'Putrajaya', 'Putrajaya', 'culture', 'Masjid Tuanku Mizan Zainal Abidin (Iron Mosque)', 'Masjid moden berstruktur keluli yang ikonik, terkenal dengan reka bentuk kontemporari. Sesuai untuk lawatan budaya dan fotografi.', 'Persiaran Persekutuan, Presint 3, 62502 Putrajaya, Wilayah Persekutuan Putrajaya, Malaysia', 2.9191718, 101.6811676, 'Daily 09:00–17:00 (visitor hours; closed during prayer times)', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/place_44_aad8660b51_20260114_162310_1cebe3.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 15:22:24', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
(45, 'Putrajaya', 'Putrajaya', 'heritage', 'Taman Warisan Pertanian (Agriculture Heritage Park)', 'Taman berkonsep warisan pertanian yang mempamerkan elemen tanaman dan pendidikan agro. Sesuai untuk lawatan keluarga dan pembelajaran asas pertanian.', 'Presint 16, 62150 Putrajaya, Wilayah Persekutuan Putrajaya, Malaysia', 2.9279160, 101.7003360, 'Daily 09:00–17:00', NULL, NULL, 5.00, 5.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_45_a8fc59b2fd_20260114_162313_0068cd.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 15:22:24', '2026-05-23 03:25:01'),
(46, 'Selangor', 'Shah Alam', 'museum', 'Sultan Alam Shah Museum', 'The Shah Alam Museum, also known as the Sultan Alam Shah Museum, is a cultural gem nestled in the heart of Selangor’s capital, offering a deep dive into the state’s rich history, heritage, and traditions. Housed in a striking modern building, the museum features a wide range of exhibits, including artifacts from Selangor’s royal family, traditional Malay weapons, ancient pottery, and displays on the state’s natural history and industrial development. The museum also showcases Selangor’s multicultural identity, with exhibits on the contributions of the Malay, Chinese, Indian, and indigenous communities to the state’s growth. Whether you’re a history enthusiast or simply curious about Selangor’s past, the Shah Alam Museum is a must-visit for an enriching and educational experience.', 'Persiaran Bandaraya, Seksyen 14, 40000 Shah Alam, Selangor', 3.0739000, 101.5183000, 'Tuesday-Sunday, 9:30 am–4:30 pm | Monday, Closed', NULL, NULL, 5.00, 5.00, 0, 'uploads/places/place_1768413945_3233.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, 'https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g298316-d4066615-Reviews-Sultan_Alam_Shah_Museum-Shah_Alam_Petaling_District_Selangor.html', NULL, 5.00, 5.00, 1, NULL, '2026-01-14 18:05:45', '2026-05-13 03:09:35'),
(47, 'Melaka', 'Melaka Tengah', 'heritage', 'The Red Square Historic Melaka (Stadthuys)', 'The \"Red House\" in Melaka refers to the iconic Stadthuys, a massive terracotta-red complex located at the heart of the historic Dutch Square. Built by the Dutch in 1650 on the ruins of a Portuguese fort, it is widely recognized as the oldest surviving Dutch colonial building in the East. For over 300 years, this striking structure—spanning nearly 50,000 square feet—served as the official residence of Dutch governors and as the administrative center for successive colonial governments. While it is famous today for its bold crimson walls, the building was actually painted white during the Dutch era; the characteristic red hue was later introduced by the British in the 19th century to create aesthetic uniformity across the district. \r\nToday, the Stadthuys serves as the History and Ethnography Museum, preserving Melaka\'s multi-layered heritage through a vast collection of artifacts, traditional costumes, and dioramas. Visitors can still admire the original Dutch architecture, characterized by thick masonry walls, heavy wooden beams, and louvered windows. The building anchors a vibrant tourist hub that includes other red-themed landmarks like the Christ Church, the Melaka Clock Tower, and the Queen Victoria Fountain, all of which contribute to the area\'s designation as a UNESCO World Heritage site. Surrounded by brightly decorated trishaws and located just steps from Jonker Street, it remains the most recognizable symbol of Melaka’s colonial past.', '31, Jalan Laksamana, Banda Hilir, 75000 Melaka', 2.1941880, 102.2490770, 'Sunday, 9 am–9 pm | Monday, Closed | Tuesday, 9 am–5:30 pm | Wednesday, 9 am–5:30 pm | Thursday, 9 am–5:30 pm | Friday, ', NULL, NULL, 0.00, 0.00, 1, 'uploads/places/suggest_1768412766_2760.jpg', NULL, NULL, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, '2026-01-15 01:21:41', '2026-04-25 17:44:50'),
